ole and aspiring for a higher role, executives will have to aspire for a new role to move ahead,&quot; he said. Younger employees may land more responsible roles earlier, with equivalent power &amp; authority &gt; Overall, the business structure has also been BIG CHANGES rejigged to reflect ve an erstwhile deputy GM in- to a role that used to earlier be filled in by a senior GM. &quot;This has given us the op- portunity to move younger pe- ople and give them roles ahead of time,&quot; he said. Business he- ads will have more flexibility as their power and authority would be related to the role. Earlier, a GM who headed a re gion would have higher sanc- tioning authority than a depu- ty GM in the same role. The other impact for emp- a customer-centric ecosystem The second big change is that business has been orga- nised around a &#39;customer eco- system&#39;. What this means is that for a set of customers, there would be a head with a composite target to offer mul- tiple products from different verticals. &quot;The ecosystems will coexist with the business verticals. For instance, a cre- dit card person will report to the corporate team, but will draw expertise from the verti- cal,&quot; said Srirang.</p>', 0, '2024-12-31 23:16:48', '1469', '1027'),
(74, 74, NULL, '<h1>From SBI To HDFC Bank: List Of Top Bank Stocks In India</h1>\r\n\r\n<h2>Under the regulation of RBI, India has a well-established banking sector with various types of banks serving the needs of individuals, businesses, and the government. And the stocks of most of the banks in India are listed, whether its the recently merged HDFC Bank, SBI, Bank of Baroda or ICICI and Axis.</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.indiatimes.com/author/vanya-gautam/5156\">Vanya Gautam</a>Updated:&nbsp;Nov 07, 2023, 18:17 IST</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2 min read</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Indiatimes\" src=\"https://im.indiatimes.in/content/2022/Mar/SBI--_621f0813773c9.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=900&amp;cc=1&amp;webp=1&amp;q=75\" style=\"height:900px; width:1200px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Under the regulation of RBI, India has a well-established banking sector with various types of banks serving the needs of individuals, businesses, and the government. And the<strong>&nbsp;stocks of most of the banks in India are listed</strong>, whether it&#39;s the recently merged&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.indiatimes.com/worth/news/why-deepak-parekh-never-owned-more-than-1-percent-in-hdfc-607835.html\" target=\"_blank\">HDFC&nbsp;</a>Bank, SBI, Bank of Baroda or ICICI and Axis.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So here&rsquo;s a list of some of the top bank stocks in India:</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>List Of Top Bank Stocks In India</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"From SBI To HDFC Bank List Of Top Bank Stocks In India\" src=\"https://im.indiatimes.in/content/2023/Nov/List-Of-Top-Bank-Stocks-In-India_654a2e6ce4bf8.jpg?w=725&amp;h=339&amp;cc=1&amp;webp=1&amp;q=75\" style=\"height:339px; width:725px\" />indiatimes</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>HDFC Bank</strong>: HDFC Bank is one of the largest and most respected private sector banks in India. HDFC Ltd had got&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.indiatimes.com/worth/news/hdfc-bank-first-financial-results-post-merger-617875.html\" target=\"_blank\">merged&nbsp;</a>with HDFC Bank in July this year.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 1,490.00</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>State Bank of India</strong>: State Bank of India is the largest public sector bank in India and is known for its extensive network and services.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 580.35</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>ICICI Bank</strong>: ICICI Bank is another major private sector bank with a significant presence in India.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 948.35</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Kotak Mahindra Bank</strong>: Kotak Mahindra Bank is known for its innovative banking solutions and customer-centric approach.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 1,753</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Axis Bank</strong>: Axis Bank is a private sector bank offering a wide range of banking and financial services.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 1,019.5</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"axis bank\" src=\"https://im.indiatimes.in/content/2022/Jul/axis-bank-robbery_62c3cf8be8ee3.jpg?w=725&amp;h=483&amp;cc=1&amp;webp=1&amp;q=75\" style=\"height:483px; width:725px\" />shutterstock</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>IndusInd Bank</strong>: IndusInd Bank is a private sector bank known for its focus on retail and corporate banking.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 1,486.45</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Bank of Baroda</strong>: Bank of Baroda is one of the leading public sector banks in India.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 191.8</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Why Has RBI Banned Bank Of Baroda From Onboaring New Customers?\" src=\"https://im.indiatimes.in/content/2023/Oct/Why-Has-RBI-Banned-Bank-Of-Baroda-From-Onboaring-New-Customers_6526500ddcca0.jpg?w=725&amp;h=338&amp;cc=1&amp;webp=1&amp;q=75\" style=\"height:338px; width:725px\" />bqprime</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Punjab National Bank</strong>: Punjab National Bank is another prominent public sector bank in India.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 76.1</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>IDFC First Bank</strong>: IDFC First Bank is known for its focus on retail banking and financial inclusion.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Current share price: Rs 83.25</p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>Disclaimer: Please keep in mind that stock performance can change rapidly, and it&#39;s important to conduct thorough research and consider current market conditions before making any investment decisions. Additionally, consult with a financial advisor to get advice based on your investment goals and risk tolerance.</em></p>', 0, '2025-01-01 01:18:03', NULL, NULL),
(75, 75, NULL, '<h1>Nifty Bank rejig today: SBI, HDFC Bank may witness over $100 million outflows amid shake-up for 12 stocks!</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Written by&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/etreporter/author-riya-sharma-479267451.cms\" target=\"_blank\">Riya Sharma</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>,&nbsp;ETMarkets.com|</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dec 31, 2024, 11:03:57 AM IST</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"The reshuffle\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818863,width-640,resizemode-4,imgsize-123066/the-reshuffle.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>1/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>The reshuffle</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The periodic rebalancing of Nifty Bank index comes into effect on Tuesday, as Nifty indices undergo their quarterly rejig to reflect India&rsquo;s evolving market dynamics. This reshuffle is set to drive $57 million in outflows into state-owned lender State Bank of India, while HDFC Bank is likely to face $59 million in outflows as institutional investors adjust portfolios, according to estimates by brokerage firm Nuvama. Here is a list of 12 stocks undergoing the Nifty Bank index reshuffle:<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>iStock</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://epaper.indiatimes.com/wealth_edition.cms?utm_source=wealth&amp;utm_medium=slideshow&amp;utm_campaign=nudge#wealthedition\"><img alt=\"Wealth edition\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-100844695,width-1280,resizemode-4/a.jpg\" style=\"height:36px; width:640px\" /></a></p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Punjab National Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818855,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-6800/punjab-national-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>2/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Punjab National Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The state-owned lender is likely to emerge as a key gainer in terms of passive inflows as a result of the Nifty Bank rejig. According to Nuvama, PNB will likely attract inflows of $25 million, driven by an increase in its weightage in the Nifty Bank Index to 2.5%.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Agencies</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"IndusInd Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818844,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-25444/indusind-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>3/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>IndusInd Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>IndusInd Bank is expected to be the second largest gainer on the Nifty Bank index as a result of the quarterly rejig. The bank will see its weightage in the Nifty Bank index rise to 4.4%, resulting in $23 million in inflows, according to Nuvama&rsquo;s estimates.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Agencies</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Federal Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818832,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-32976/federal-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>4/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Federal Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Federal Bank is expected to see its weightage in the Nifty Bank index increase to 3.4%, likely resulting in $18 million in inflows, according to Nuvama&rsquo;s estimates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ETMarkets.com</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://popup.taboola.com/en/?template=colorbox&amp;utm_source=timesinternetlimited-economictimes&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=thumbnails-300x250:Mid%20Photo%20Thumbnails%201:\" target=\"_blank\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://popup.taboola.com/en/?template=colorbox&amp;utm_source=timesinternetlimited-economictimes&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=thumbnails-300x250:Mid%20Photo%20Thumbnails%201:\" target=\"_blank\">by Taboola</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>You May Like<a href=\"https://www.upgrad.com/doctor-of-business-administration-from-esgci/?utm_source=taboola&amp;utm_medium=partner&amp;utm_campaign=IND_ACQ_WEB_TABOOLA_PARTNER_MV_ESGCI_DBA_T1_D_OND24&amp;utm_content=timesinternetlimited-economictimes&amp;utm_term=http%3A%2F%2Fcdn.taboola.com%2Flibtrc%2Fstatic%2Fthumbnails%2F44d76f90e8a123aa66ff0ead3d97037c.png&amp;tblci=GiCMacJrsp41tEvLSPCBLUEfm785nQ1tk0TNHyUzvk6gBCCng1kotdCZvuDB_Pj3ATDegGQ#tblciGiCMacJrsp41tEvLSPCBLUEfm785nQ1tk0TNHyUzvk6gBCCng1kotdCZvuDB_Pj3ATDegGQ\" target=\"_blank\">Start an independent career with a DoctorateupGrad|</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://popup.taboola.com/en/?template=colorbox&amp;utm_source=timesinternetlimited-economictimes&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=thumbnails-300x250:Mid%20Photo%20Thumbnails%201:\" target=\"_blank\">Sponsored</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Learn More</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Bank of Baroda\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818810,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-67880/bank-of-baroda.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>5/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Bank of Baroda</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Bank of Baroda is likely to witness $17 million in inflows, buoyed by an increase in its weightage in the Nifty Bank index to 3.3%.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ETMarkets.com</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Canara Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818779,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-9920/canara-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>6/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Canara Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Canara Bank is expected to see its weightage in the Nifty Bank index increase to 2.4%, likely resulting in $13 million in inflows, according to Nuvama&rsquo;s estimates.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Agencies</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"AU Small Finance Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818757,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-13634/au-small-finance-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>7/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>AU Small Finance Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>AU Small Finance Bank is likely to witness $12 million in inflows, driven by an uptick in its weightage in the Nifty Bank index to 2.2%.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Agencies</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"ICICI Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818747,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-1201457/icici-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>8/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>ICICI Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Lending giant ICICI Bank is expected to witness its weightage in the Nifty Bank index increase to 25.2%, likely resulting in $10 million in inflows, according to Nuvama&rsquo;s estimates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ETMarkets.com</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Axis Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818735,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-73448/axis-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>9/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Axis Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Axis Bank is likely to witness $9 million in inflows, driven by a rise in its weightage in the Nifty Bank index to 8.6%.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Reuters</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"IDFC First Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818731,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-88170/idfc-first-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>10/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>IDFC First Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>IDFC First Bank is expected to witness its weightage in the Nifty Bank index increase to 2.7%, likely resulting in $9 million in inflows, according to Nuvama&rsquo;s estimates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ETMarkets.com</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"HDFC Bank \" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818721,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-97066/hdfc-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>11/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>HDFC Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Private lender HDFC Bank will face reductions in its weightage in the Nifty Bank index to 28.2%, leading to significant outflows of $59 million, according to Nuvama&rsquo;s estimates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Agencies</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"SBI Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818703,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-10550/sbi-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>12/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>SBI Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The state-owned lender is expected to witness its weightage in the Nifty Bank index decrease to 8.6%, likely resulting in $57 million in outflows, according to Nuvama&rsquo;s estimates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ETMarkets.com</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Kotak Mahindra Bank\" src=\"https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-116818686,width-640,height-480,resizemode-75,imgsize-32008/kotak-mahindra-bank.jpg\" style=\"height:480px; width:640px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>13/13</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Kotak Mahindra Bank</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Kotak Mahindra Bank is likely to see $19 million in outflows, driven by a decline in its weightage in the Nifty Bank index to 8.6%.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n(<strong>Disclaimer</strong>: Recommendations, suggestions, views and opinions given by the experts are their own. These do not represent the views of The Economic Times)</p>', 0, '2025-01-01 01:20:10', NULL, NULL),
(76, 76, 217, '<p>ICICI Bank junks ranks, scraps exec symbols Flattens Top Mgmt Structure By Removing All Designations Of Deputy GM And Above Mayur.Shetty @timesgroup.com Mumbai: In a major HR shift, ICICI Bank has flattened its top management by getting rid of all grades of deputy ge- neral manager (GM) and abo- ve. Management executives are now known by their role and there are no grade-based benefits. The bank has also got rid of all symbols of hie- rarchy no longer can anyo- ne guess an executive&#39;s senio- rity based on the size of his car or access to the executive dining room. This is a big shift for a bank where even the internet bandwidth earlier depended on seniority. The move will impact over 400 executives of the level of deputy GM, joint GM, GM and senior GMs. This is the first major change in HR policy since Sandeep Bakhshi took charge as CEO last year. &quot;We have recently reorga- nised ourselves to work toget- her seamlessly across func- tional and departmental bo- undaries in order to maximi- se our share of market opportunities. We have mo- ved to role-based designa- tions from grade-based struc- tures and empowered our te- ams at the local level,&quot; Bakh- shi told analysts recently. &quot;If we have to be agile and nimble-footed, we cannot re- main a hierarchical organisa- tion. Because of the grades, these structures and levels got hard-coded and there was a sense of hierarchy,&quot; said group HR chief T K Srirang. Following the shift, the bank will have the flexibility to mo- ICICI Bank will now have role- based designations instead of a grade-based structure So even a deputy GM can be assigned a senior GM&#39;s role, removing all sense of hierarchy There won&#39;t be any regular promotions automatically loyees is that there will be no automatic promotion based on the period of service. &quot;In any organisation in India, there is an expectation that every three-four years there would be a promotion. Now, instead of sitting in the same role and aspiring for a higher role, executives will have to aspire for a new role to move ahead,&quot; he said. Younger employees may land more responsible roles earlier, with equivalent power &amp; authority &gt; Overall, the business structure has also been BIG CHANGES rejigged to reflect ve an erstwhile deputy GM in- to a role that used to earlier be filled in by a senior GM. &quot;This has given us the op- portunity to move younger pe- ople and give them roles ahead of time,&quot; he said. Business he- ads will have more flexibility as their power and authority would be related to the role. Earlier, a GM who headed are gion would have higher sanc- tioning authority than a depu- ty GM in the same role. The other impact for emp- a customer-centric ecosystem The second big change is that business has been orga- nised around a &#39;customer eco- system&#39;. What this means is that for a set of customers, there would be a head with a composite target to offer mul- tiple products from different verticals. &quot;The ecosystems will coexist with the business verticals. For instance, a cre- dit card person will report to the corporate team, but will draw expertise from the verti- cal,&quot; said Srirang.</p>', 5, '2025-01-01 01:22:13', '1469', '1027'),
(77, 77, 218, '<p>ICICI Bank seeks to digitise 100 villages in 100 days TIMES NEWS NETWORK &egrave; Mumbai: ICICI Bank on Mon- -day said it will run a project to transform 100 villages across the country into digital villages in as many days. The project S e envisages enabling vil- 1 lagers to use digital channels for banking 3 and payment transactions. &#39; ICICI Bank will open acco unts for all and enable cashless payments to retail stores thro- - ugh messaging-based applica- r tions that can run on basic pho 1 4 nes. &quot;Besides creating a cash- less payment system, we will provide vocational training and credit linkages to make villages digital,&quot; said Chanda Koch- har, MD &amp; CEO, ICICI Bank. She added that the bank would draw from its experiences in Akodara village in Guja- rat&#39;s Sabrakanta district where it ran a pilot pro- ject on digital villages. In the next 100 days, the bank will provide vo- cational training to 10,000 underprivileged villa- gers from largely agrarian sta- tes The announcement is part of the bank&#39;s continuing effort to provide a digital ecosystem across the country, including rural India, in the wake of de monetisation of high value cur- rencies, Kochhar said. To provi- de mobile banking access to the underprivileged, the bank plans to use SMS and USSD banking solutions. USSD (Unst- ructured Supplementary Ser- vice Data) is a technology that enables communication betwe- en the mobile phone and the bank&#39;s servers in a manner si- milar to how a mobile user checks his balance talktime. In the first phase, ICICI Bank will use tablet-based banking and Aadhaar-based e-KYC to help villagers open accounts without submitting physical documents. All adults in the villages will ha- ve savings accounts, which will be linked to Aadhaar to enable direct transfer of go- vernment benefits.</p>', 2, '2025-01-01 01:25:29', '631', '847'),
(78, 78, 220, '<p>Axis to buy Citi&#39;s retail biz for *12,325 crore To gain big in credit cards; regulatory approvals likely in 9-12 months MANOJIT SAHA Mumbai, 30 March DEAL DYNAMICS xis Bank, the third-largest What Axis is getting from the Citi deal private sector lender in the country, will buy the retail business of Citibank India in an all-cash deal for 12,325 crore. This is the biggest deal in the banking space since the acquisition of ING Vysya Bank by Kotak Mahindra Bank in 2014, which was valued at 15,000 crore. The deal includes Citi&#39;s credit cards, retail banking, wealth manage- ment, and consumer loan businesses, PAGE II,1 CITI DEAL, A PROFITABLE BUY FOR AXIS BANK besides the con- sumer business of its non-banking financial company, Citicorp Finance (India) Limited. This, however, excludes Citi&#39;s insti- tutional client businesses in India, Citi said in a statement, adding that Axis Bank was selected following an exten- sive and competitive auction process. Citi said it remained committed to serving institutional clients in India and globally. Axis Bank will offer 3,600 employ- ees of Citi&#39;s consumer banking busi- ness a remuneration that is at par or higher than their current packages. For Citi, the sale is part of Chief Executive Jane Fraser&#39;s plan to over- haul its business by exiting retail banking operations in 13 countries ▶3 mn customers of Citibank India 2.5 mn credit card holders (credit card customer base to rise by 31%) 1.11 trn AUM from Citi Wealth and Private banking Deposits of 50,200 cr; 81% are low-cost current &amp; savings account deposits ▶Salary accounts of 1,600 corporates with over 1 million customers and average salary of *70,000/month ▶7 offices, 21 branches, and 499 ATMs across 18 cities ▶3,600 employees of Citi&#39;s consumer bank ▶Post acquisition, Axis Bank&#39;s deposit base will increase by 7%; CASA by 12%, and loan 4% Major credit HDFC Bank 16.27 card players Cards issued as of February 2022 (in million) SBI Card 13.52 ICICI Bank 12.77 Axis Bank 8.6 Citi India 2.55 Source: RBI &quot;THE ACQUISITION STRENGTHENS OUR MARKET POSITION, REDUCES THE GAP IN KEY SEGMENTS WITH PEERS, AND PROVIDES AN OPPORTUNITY TO ACCELERATE RETAIL BUSINESS GROWTH&quot; Amitabh Chaudhry, MD &amp; CEO, Axis Bank PAGE 4 WHEN LIFE COMES FULL CIRCLE WITH CITI DEAL where it does not have the necessary with our broader strategic reposition- scale to compete. &quot;As we move forward with this transaction, India remains a key insti- tutional market for Citi,&quot; said Peter Babej, Citi Asia Pacific CEO. &quot;In line ing, we will continue to support our institutional clients in this core market and across APAC, delivering the full power of our global network to enable their growth,&quot; he added. Turn to Page 6 ▸</p>', 6, '2025-01-01 01:30:58', '1280', '1115'),
