ird largest with AUM of 8.8 lakh crore, stood at 1.11 lakh crore &quot;Over the past several years, asset management businesses have grown at healthy rates while requiring mini- mal incremental capital,&quot; said Shah. &quot;Businesses that deliver consistent growth without heavy capital deploy ment tend to command higher valuation multiples.&quot; Prudential Corporation Holdings, the joint venture partner in the com- pany will offload up to 14.41% of ICICI Prudential AMC&#39;s equity Since the issue is entirely an offer for sale (OFS) by Prudential, the company will not receive any proceeds from the IPO. Shah said Prudential&#39;s decision to sell a stake in the AMC in the IPO has come after remaining invested in the business since 1998. &quot;They are monetising a part of their investment after 27 years and are sel- ling only a portion,&quot; he said. ICICI Bank will continue to be the majority shareholder of the firm with a 53% stake in the joint venture, said Shah. BUSINESS STRATEGY ICICI Prudential&#39;s focus on hybrid products has made it one of the big- gest asset managers in the category Its market share in the hybrid cate- gory is around 25% compared to 13.6% in equity assets and 13.6% ove rall. &quot;Our strength in hybrid and as- set allocation-oriented strategies. has been built over multiple market cycles by focusing on risk-adjusted returns,&quot; said Shah. It is also sharpening its focus on the alternative investment business in- cluding equity-focused Portfolio Ma- nagement Services (PMS), Alternati- ve Investment Funds (AIFs), private credit, and office yield funds. Shah said between FY23 and FY25, al- ternative AUM has registered a com- pounded annual growth rate of 43.3%. Currently mutual funds account for 93% of its assets while alternatives ac- count for the balance 7%.</p>', 1, '2025-12-23 04:08:14', '492', '679'),
(100, 101, 340, '<p>Tata Motors is offering massive discounts of up to Rs 1.75 lakh on its cars in November 2025. The list of models includes Harrier, Safari, Curvv, Altroz, and more. The offers by the brand on these models include cash discounts, exchange bonuses, corporate offers, and more, depending on the dealership. All of this comes while the automaker is preparing to launch its new Sierra in the country. Here we take a look at the offers on various models on sale. Tata Harrier, Safari Tata dealerships are offering mid-spec Adventure trims for the Harrier and Safari with discounts of up to Rs 1.75 lakh. The entry-level Smart trims have discounts of up to Rs 50,000, while the lower-spec Pure trims enjoy benefits totaling Rs 1.25 lakh.</p>', 0, '2026-01-08 01:01:06', '614', '965'),
(101, 102, 355, '<p>ICICI Pru AMC becomes most valued stock in capital mkt sector Stock closes 19% higher post debut; market cap overtakes HDFC AMC SAMIE MODAK Mumbai, 19 December Shares of ICICI Prudential Asset Management Company (AMC) surged as much as 23 per cent in their trading debut on Friday, as investors bet on the company as a key beneficiary of the ongoing shift in house- hold savings from traditional assets to equities. The stock touched an intraday high of 2,663, before settling at *2,576, up *411, or 19 per cent, over its issue price of *2,165 per share. At close, ICICI Prudential AMC commanded a market capitalisation of 1.27 trillion, making it the most valued AMC stock in India&#39;s capital market sector, overtaking peer HDFC AMC, which is currently valued at 1.14 trillion. The strong listing followed robust demand for the asset manager&#39;s 10,602-crore initial public offering, which was sub- scribed nearly 40 times and garnered bids worth about 3 trillion. The issue was entirely an offer for sale by UK-based Prudential Plc ICICI Pruden- tial AMC&#39;s joint venture partner. The company had priced its shares at around 40 times its financial year 2025 (FY25) earn- ings, broadly in line with listed Proud peers such as HDFC AMC and Nippon Life AMC. Analysts, however, said ICICI Prudential AMC merited a valuation pre- mium, given its leadership in active equity assets under management (AUM), superior revenue mix, margins, and return on equity (ROE). &quot;The attractiveness of the AMC industry in general, driven by financialisation as a long-term macro theme, the strong operating performance of ICICI Prudential AMC, and the pricing of the deal at an attractive discount to listed peers make it one of the most compelling IPOS of the year,&quot; wrote Himanshu Dugar of Stylus Holdings in an IPO note published on Smartkarma. &quot;We expect a listing pop of 15-20 Strong debut ICICI Prudential AMC (*) 2,800 2,586.7 2,600 Change A19.5% 2,400 -2,165.0 Issue price 22001 2.000 Dec 19,25 Source Bloomberg Compiled by BS Research Bureau percent as the stock catches up to relative valuations, with further upside as free float increases.&quot; Ahead of the IPO, ICICI Bank held a 51 per cent stake in the company, while Prudential owned the remaining 49 per cent. Post listing, Prudential&#39;s stake has declined to 35 per cent, taking the combined pro- moter holding to about 86 per cent. AMCS typically operate asset-light, high-margin busi- nesses, translating into strong profitability metrics. ICICI Pru- dential AMC reported an ROE of 83 per cent in financial year 2025 (FY25). Net profit stood at 2,650 crore, while AUM surged to about *9.1 trillion from 26.5 trillion a year earlier. Groww gets Jefferies&#39; &#39;buy&#39; initiation Shares of Groww oper- ator Billionbrains Garage Ventures jumped 12 per cent on Friday after Jef- feries initiated coverage on the investment plat- form with a &#39;buy&#39; rating, citing its rapid rise and strong earnings growth visibility. Shares of the company ended at 161, up 17, or 11.8 per cent. The brokerage has set a price target of 180, implying an upside of about 12 per cent from current levels. Jefferies expects Groww&#39;s earnings per share to grow at a com- pounded annual rate of 35 per cent between financial year 2026 (FY26) and FY28, driven by steady growth in the core broking business, expansion in new rev- enue streams, such as margin trading facility and wealth manage- ment, and margin expan- sion of around 700 basis points from FY26 levels. BS REPORTER</p>', 5, '2026-01-15 21:46:04', '743', '695'),
(102, 103, NULL, '<p>ICICI Prudential Mutual Fund announces change in fund managers of its 2 funds<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ICICI Prudential Mutual Fund announces a shift in leadership for its funds. S Naren will transition out of the Dynamic Asset Allocation Active FOF management. Concurrently, expect updates to the Gold ETF, Regular Gold Savings Fund, and Silver ETF Fund of Fund&#39;s core attributes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/icici-prudential-mutual-fund/mutual_funds_search/amcid-14.cms\" target=\"_blank\">ICICI Prudential Mutual Fund</a>&nbsp;has announced change in fund managers of its two funds -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/topic/icici-prudential-business-cycle-fund\" target=\"_blank\">ICICI Prudential Business Cycle Fund</a>&nbsp;and ICICI Prudential Dynamic Asset Allocation Active FOF.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe changes are effective from January 1, 2026. The fund house informed about these changes through a notice cum addendum.According to the notice cum addendum, ICICI Prudential Dynamic Asset Allocation Active FOF which was previously managed by Sankaran Naren, Dharmesh Kakkad, Manish Bhantia, and Ritesh Lunawat will now be managed by Dharmesh Kakkad, Manish Bhantia, Ritesh Lunawat, and Sharmila D&rsquo;silva with&nbsp;<a href=\"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/topic/s-naren\" target=\"_blank\">S Naren</a>&nbsp;no longer part of this team.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOther fund - ICICI Prudential Business Cycle Fund which was previously managed by Anish Tawakley,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/topic/manish-banthia\" target=\"_blank\">Manish Banthia</a>, and Manan Tijoriwala will now be managed by Anish Tawakley, Manish Banthia, Manan Tijoriwala, and Divya Jain.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs of November 30, 2025 (last available portfolio), ICICI Prudential Dynamic Asset Allocation Active FOF had an AUM of Rs 28,974 crore and ICICI Prudential Business Cycle Fund had an AUM of Rs 15,708 crore.</p>', 0, '2026-01-15 21:48:34', NULL, NULL),
(103, 104, NULL, '<h1>Tata MF launches Titanium Specialised Investment Fund; check key features</h1>\r\n\r\n<h2>According to the SID, the Titanium Specialised Investment Fund (SIF) is suitable for medium- to long-term capital appreciation</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Mutual fund\" src=\"https://bsmedia.business-standard.com/_media/bs/img/article/2025-11/06/full/1762451262-1673.jpg?im=FeatureCrop,size=(826,465)\" style=\"height:465px; width:826px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.business-standard.com/author/si-reporter\">SI Reporter</a>&nbsp;New Delhi</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4 min read&nbsp;Last Updated :&nbsp;Nov 24 2025 | 11:47 AM&nbsp;IST</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://news.google.com/publications/CAAqBwgKMLC13Qowpt3RAQ?hl=en-IN&amp;gl=IN&amp;ceid=IN:en\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Google News\" src=\"https://www.business-standard.com/assets/web-assets/images/googleNews.svg\" /></a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Listen to This Article</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Play</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1x<img alt=\"Arrow Icon\" src=\"https://www.business-standard.com/assets/web-assets/icons/icon-arrow-down.png\" style=\"height:24px; width:24px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Tata Asset Management has launched a new investment product, the Titanium Specialised Investment Fund (SIF), offered under&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.business-standard.com/topic/tata-mutual-fund\" target=\"_blank\">Tata Mutual Fund</a>. The fund, which employs a hybrid long-short investment strategy, aims to dynamically combine equity, debt, and derivative exposures to help investors navigate multiple market phases while seeking better risk-adjusted returns. The New Fund Offer (NFO) opens on November 24, 2025, and will close on December 8, 2025.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><small>&nbsp;</small></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Designed for investors with a higher risk appetite, the fund requires a minimum investment of ₹10 lakh across all SIFs at the PAN level with the asset management company. The fund follows a hybrid long-short structure, maintaining at least 25 per cent allocation each to equities and debt, with a maximum 25 per cent unhedged exposure to short instruments.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;<small>&nbsp;</small></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&ldquo;This unique mix allows the fund to participate in market upswings through long positions in equity and derivative instruments, cushion downside risks via short strategies and arbitrage, and potentially generate returns through debt. The strategy can also invest in&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.business-standard.com/topic/reit\" target=\"_blank\">Real Estate Investment Trusts (REITs)</a>&nbsp;and Infrastructure Investment Trusts (InvITs),&rdquo; Tata Asset Management said in a release.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Investment structure</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>According to the Scheme Information Document (SID), units of the Titanium SIF will have a face value of ₹10 per unit. During the NFO period, investors must commit a minimum of ₹10 lakh, and additional investments can be made in multiples of ₹1 thereafter.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><small>&nbsp;</small></p>\r\n\r\n<p>On a continuous basis, according to SID, the same minimum and incremental investment norms apply across all Titanium SIF strategies at the PAN level. The fund has a perpetual duration with no lock-in period, offering flexibility to investors.</p>', 0, '2026-01-15 21:54:47', NULL, NULL),
(104, 105, 359, '<p>Tata Motors Q3 Profit Rises Il-fold on Strong India Show But net at *1,215 cr misses estimates on lax JLR business even as domestic strategy bears fruits Our Bureau Mumbal: Tata Motors reported anearly 11-fold increase in conso- lidated net profit for the quarter through December, led mainly by strong volumes from its Indi- an operations. But the perfor mance missed analyst estimates by half, owing to a lax quarter for the Jaguar Land Rover business. Consolidated net profit for the October-December quarter rose to 1,215 crore from about 112 cro- re a year earlier, as the company sald Its turnaround strategy here started to bear fruits and due to cost controls. Consolidated reve nue increased 14% to 74,156 crore. The turnaround strategy was implemented in August to turn around the company&#39;s passenger vehicles business as well as to strengthen Its position as the market leader in the commercial vehicles segment. Analysts tracked by Bloomberg on average were expecting Tata Motors to post a net profit of &euro;2,500 crore. The UK-based Jaguar Land Ro ver unit, the biggest money-spin- Miles to Go Analysts were 3.5% retail sales 14% expecting co to post a growth due to China, net profit of 25k cr overseas markets carmaker&#39;s consolidated JLR posted revenue touched &lt;74,156 crore flat sales in a few markets like the UK, US ner for Tata Motors, posted flat sa- les In a few markets like the UK, USand mainland Europe, keeping the consolidated performance be low estimates. Its retail sales grew 3.5%, driven primarily by China and overseas markets. Investments made in new pro- ducts, technology and capacities also welghed on the margin. In the standalone Indian bust- ness, sales volume, including ex- ports, rose 31% to 172,952 units in the past quarter, with significant growth across the entire portfo- lio. In passenger vehicles, for long a drag on the overall bust ness, India sales rose 22%. 31% Standalone Indian business, sales volume, Including exports, touched 172,952 units In the past quarter &quot;The turnaround strategy is de Ilvering results for us as is evi- dent in share gain in an intensely competitive market and impro ved profitability enabled by a slew of new product launches and customer-centric incentives,&quot; managing director Guenter But schek said in a news release. Jaguar Land Rover, meanwhile, is expecting an improved perfor mance in the ongoing quarter. JLR will soon be launching its first electric car and expects a &quot;stronger all-round performan- ce in the fourth quarter, driven by new models, seasonality and improved profitability,&quot; said Ralph Speth, the UK-based unit&#39;s chief executive. Consolidated finance costs on a consolidated level rose to 1,247 crore from 377 crore a year earli- er due to increased borrowings In both in India and at JLR. The com- pany&#39;s consolidated net debt stood at 47,777 crore primarily due to higher investments in JLR. ET Analysis +11 Get a dally mall with the most Important news on the automotive Industry from all media outlets. Send a blank mall to join@etauto.com to sign up.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Tata Motors Q3 Profit Rises Il-fold on Strong India Show But net at *1,215 cr misses estimates on lax JLR business even as domestic strategy bears fruits Our Bureau Mumbal: Tata Motors reported anearly 11-fold increase in conso- lidated net profit for the quarter through December, led mainly by strong volumes from its Indi- an operations. But the perfor mance missed analyst estimates by half, owing to a lax quarter for the Jaguar Land Rover business. Consolidated net profit for the October-December quarter rose to 1,215 crore from about 112 cro- re a year earlier, as the company sald Its turnaround strategy here started to bear fruits and due to cost controls. Consolidated reve nue increased 14% to 74,156 crore. The turnaround strategy was implemented in August to turn around the company&#39;s passenger vehicles business as well as to strengthen Its position as the market leader in the commercial vehicles segment. Analysts tracked by Bloomberg on average were expecting Tata Motors to post a net profit of &euro;2,500 crore. The UK-based Jaguar Land Ro ver unit, the biggest money-spin- Miles to Go Analysts were 3.5% retail sales 14% expecting co to post a growth due to China, net profit of 25k cr overseas markets carmaker&#39;s consolidated JLR posted revenue touched &lt;74,156 crore flat sales in a few markets like the UK, US ner for Tata Motors, posted flat sa- les In a few markets like the UK, USand mainland Europe, keeping the consolidated performance be low estimates. Its retail sales grew 3.5%, driven primarily by China and overseas markets. Investments made in new pro- ducts, technology and capacities also welghed on the margin. In the standalone Indian bust- ness, sales volume, including ex- ports, rose 31% to 172,952 units in the past quarter, with significant growth across the entire portfo- lio. In passenger vehicles, for long a drag on the overall bust ness, India sales rose 22%. 31% Standalone Indian business, sales volume, Including exports, touched 172,952 units In the past quarter &quot;The turnaround strategy is de Ilvering results for us as is evi- dent in share gain in an intensely competitive market and impro ved profitability enabled by a slew of new product launches and customer-centric incentives,&quot; managing director Guenter But schek said in a news release. Jaguar Land Rover, meanwhile, is expecting an improved perfor mance in the ongoing quarter. JLR will soon be launching its first electric car and expects a &quot;stronger all-round performan- ce in the fourth quarter, driven by new models, seasonality and improved profitability,&quot; said Ralph Speth, the UK-based unit&#39;s chief executive. Consolidated finance costs on a consolidated level rose to 1,247 crore from 377 crore a year earli- er due to increased borrowings In both in India and at JLR. The com- pany&#39;s consolidated net d